{"name":"Codex Grey","hex":"#9c9c9c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"codex","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An early manuscript book, especially one bound in the modern manner, by joining pages, as opposed to a rolled scroll.","An official list of medicines and medicinal ingredients."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/codex"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Codex","blocks":[{"text":"The codex was the historical ancestor format of the modern book. Technically, the vast majority of modern books use the codex format, of a stack of pages bound at one edge. However, the term codex is usually reserved for older manuscript books, which mostly used sheets of vellum, parchment, or papyrus, rather than paper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Devil_codex_Gigas.jpg/330px-Devil_codex_Gigas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codex"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/2049_-_Byzantine_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Parchement_scroll%2C_13th_century_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg/500px-2049_-_Byzantine_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Parchement_scroll%2C_13th_century_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/2049_-_Byzantine_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Parchement_scroll%2C_13th_century_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg/500px-2049_-_Byzantine_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Parchement_scroll%2C_13th_century_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall%27Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The scroll was the document form which was replaced by the codex during the late Roman Empire.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2049_-_Byzantine_Museum%2C_Athens_-_Parchement_scroll%2C_13th_century_-_Photo_by_Giovanni_Dall'Orto%2C_Nov_12.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Replica_of_roman_wax_writing_tablet_with_stylus.jpg/500px-Replica_of_roman_wax_writing_tablet_with_stylus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Replica_of_roman_wax_writing_tablet_with_stylus.jpg/1280px-Replica_of_roman_wax_writing_tablet_with_stylus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Replica_of_roman_wax_writing_tablet_with_stylus.jpg/500px-Replica_of_roman_wax_writing_tablet_with_stylus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reproduction Roman-style wax tablet, from which the codex evolved","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReplica_of_roman_wax_writing_tablet_with_stylus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Facsimile_of_the_book_of_kells-Interior_of_the_Old_Library%2C_Trinity_College%2C_Dublin.jpg/500px-Facsimile_of_the_book_of_kells-Interior_of_the_Old_Library%2C_Trinity_College%2C_Dublin.jpg?utm_sourc